tached as `TASK-260916-97dhxd_review-verdict-rev1.md`. The Change Request CR-TASK-260916-97dhxd-1 revision 1 was not accepted. `repeat-of: none`.\n\n**What I verified myself**\n\n- Working tree re-hashed to the candidate tree OID before review.\n- Core package tests rerun: 45 of 45 green.\n- Release build rerun from a scratch copy: BUILD SUCCEEDED. The composed Info.plist carries no client ID key and no secret-shaped keys. Binary strings carry no PAT or private-key material.\n- Producer mutants M1 to M8 and M9d are genuine narrowing mutants with named failing tests. The M9 and M9c survivors are honestly bounded. I accepted that evidence.\n\n**Findings that block acceptance**\n\n- **No session restore from Keychain.** The session lives only in memory. After relaunch the UI shows disconnected, the 30-second sync loop never runs, and logout cannot delete the persisted token pair. Tokens stay in Keychain indefinitely, which contradicts the design's \"log out on this Mac removes local tokens\".\n- **Flow-level token refresh is never driven.** My mutant that stops the Flow from ever refreshing an expiring token survived all 45 tests. The AC row for refresh concurrency is covered only at the helper, not at the production call site in `currentToken`.\n- **PAT guard narrowed on the refresh path survives.** My mutant admitting fine-grained PAT-shaped tokens in the refresh response survived. Only the device poll and API client paths have negative tests.\n- **Audit and redaction guards have no production callers.** The outcome claims secret enforcement through them, but neither is invoked outside tests.\n- **Public client ID binding must ship in the next revision.** Per the coordinator directive on this run, the now-attached public client ID must become the product default in the generator input, with Project.swift regenerated and the build rerun. The producer's prompt did not include the binding, so this is rework, not an external blocker. The generator is not installed in this environment, so I could not run it either.\n\n**Accepted as-is:** Device Flow transport behavior, cancellation, in-session logout, 401 and 403 handling with local control preserved, no PAT UI, no secrets in Relux state or the logger, management window composition, menu changes, and the new spec files.\n\n**Skipped:** the `logbook` command is not installed here, so no logbook entry was written. The full finding text with the required tests for each item is on the board in the verdict resource.","ttft_ms":1332,"type":"result","duration_ms":524547,"uuid":"e1f73cfa-9ff6-4548-8622-8a0d934c1562","ttft_stream_ms":1165,"time_to_request_ms":91,"first_content_frame_ms":1166,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
